kosha control-systems

  -- control systems: engineering the behaviour of dynamic systems over time.
  -- the discipline of making systems do what you want despite disturbances.
  -- a thermostat is a control system. so is autopilot, ABS, and insulin pump.
  --
  -- open-loop vs closed-loop:
  --   open-loop:   no feedback. output not measured. toaster, washing machine timer.
  --                predictable only if system is well-modelled. no disturbance rejection.
  --   closed-loop: feedback. output measured and compared to desired (setpoint).
  --                error = setpoint - actual output.
  --                controller adjusts input based on error → error → 0.
  --
  -- PID controller: the workhorse of industrial control.
  --   P (proportional): u = Kp × e.     proportional to current error.
  --                     large Kp → fast response, may overshoot.
  --   I (integral):     u = Ki × ∫e dt.  integral of past error.
  --                     eliminates steady-state error (I action catches constant offset).
  --   D (derivative):   u = Kd × de/dt.  rate of change of error.
  --                     anticipates future error → reduces overshoot.
  --   PID combined: u = Kp×e + Ki×∫e + Kd×ė
  --   tuning: choosing Kp, Ki, Kd for stable, fast, accurate response.
  --   Ziegler-Nichols method: systematic tuning from step response.
  --
  -- transfer function: H(s) = Y(s)/X(s) in Laplace domain.
  --   poles: values of s where H(s) → ∞. determine stability.
  --   zeros: values of s where H(s) = 0. determine frequency response.
  --   stable system: all poles in left half of s-plane (negative real part).
  --
  -- Bode plot: gain and phase vs frequency. shows stability margins.
  --   gain margin: how much gain before instability.
  --   phase margin: how much phase lag before instability.
  --   60° phase margin: well-damped. < 30°: risk of oscillation.

  "signal-varga-vishesa"
  "engineering-varga-vishesa"
  "subanta-swarupa"

  "feedback-swarupa"
  "derivative-yukta antiderivative-yukta"  -- PID uses both
  "fourier-engineering-yukta"
  "laplace-yukta"

done
